import Gimle.Forseti.PolynomialTrapping
import Gimle.Forseti.Examples.GalerkinNS.K5

-- the closed forms below have hundreds of rational terms; elaborating them needs room
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

/-! # The 5-mode member below `E ≤ 6`: a degree-4 tube around its rotating wave

For `K5` (`ν = 1/10`, `f = 1`, start `(1, …, 1)`) every set a global decrease traps
contains the laminar point (`E = 25/2`), and no quadratic form about a centre was
found below it either (gimle-forseti's spike 213). This module traps a sublevel set
`V ≤ 1` of a **degree-4** polynomial, a thin tube around the member's attractor — in
simulation a rotating wave of energy `≈ 4.75` (not a Lean statement) — on which
`V' ≤ α (inner − V)` holds with `inner < 1` by an explicit sum of squares with an
S-procedure multiplier `σ ≥ 0`: `β − αV − V' + σ (V − 1)` is a sum of squares
everywhere, so on the set, where `σ (V − 1) ≤ 0`, the decrease holds. The set lies
in `{E ≤ 6}` by an S-lemma certificate, so the energy observation stays in
`[0, 6]` for all time: the level of the member's standing undecided claim, below
the laminar `25/2` and the family bound `13`.

The decrease certificate is written as the columns of a rounded Cholesky factor of
the Gram matrix less `ε I` (`sq…`) with the exact remainder absorbed pair by pair
(`rem…`), since an exact `LDLᵀ` of a 56×56 matrix has thousand-digit entries. All
numbers are rational; every identity is `ring`. -/

